<title>FRANCE: Israeli author David Shahar dies in Paris.</title>
<headline>Israeli author David Shahar dies in Paris.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israeli author David Shahar, best known internationally for his collection of short stories in Hebrew &quot;Stories from Jerusalem&quot;, has died in Paris aged 71, friends said.</p>
<p>The book recounted the lives of &quot;small people&quot;, often living on the fringes of society in the author's native city.</p>
<p>Shahar, who won the prestigious French Prix Medicis Etranger for his novel &quot;The Day of the Countess&quot;, died of illness on Wednesday.</p>
